Of course. Here is a well-designed, reusable hook for API calls in React using TanStack Query.
This hook, useApi, abstracts the logic for both querying (GET) and mutating (POST, PUT, DELETE) data, providing a single, consistent interface for all your API interactions. 🚀
1. API Client Setup (apiClient.js)
First, it's a best practice to centralize your API client configuration. This allows you to set a base URL, headers, and interceptors in one place. We'll use axios for this.
// src/lib/apiClient.js
import axios from 'axios';

// Create an Axios instance
const apiClient = axios.create({
  baseURL: 'https://api.example.com', // Replace with your API's base URL
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
  },
});

// You can also add interceptors for handling tokens, errors, etc.
apiClient.interceptors.request.use((config) => {
  // const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
